{"id":25657,"title":"A Case Study of Isosurface Extraction Algorithm Performance","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-7091-6783-0_26","final_url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/15006491","year":2000,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":"10.1007/978-3-7091-6783-0_26","arxiv":null,"sha256":"f9acad0dfc7b726c4787dd6a03d4187d1a9a1653b9ec999b6f764c2b0eaeddca","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793059862.5195112,"text_chars":29541,"abstract":"Isosurface extraction is an important and useful visualization method. Over the past ten years, the field has seen numerous isosurface techniques published, leaving the user in a quandary about which one should be used. Some papers have published complexity analysis of the techniques, yet empirical evidence comparing different methods is lacking. This case study presents a comparative study of several representative isosurface extraction algorithms. It reports and analyzes empirical measurements of execution times and memory behavior for each algorithm. The results show that asymptotically optimal techniques may not be the best choice when implemented on modern computer architectures.Joint Eurographics - IEEE TCVG Symposium on Visualizatio","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/15006491","https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-7091-6783-0_26","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/m2/1/high_res_d/15006491.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=marching cubes","https://core.ac.uk/works/163094918","https://core.ac.uk/download/276285697.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=isosurface extraction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=isosurface rendering without mesh","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=lorensen cline marching cubes","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=marching cubes edge completeness","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=isosurface point indexing","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=span space isosurface extraction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=extract isosurface from volume","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=optimal isosurface extraction interval trees","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=span space algorithm volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=marching cubes cell extraction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=fast marching cubes algorithm","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=fast shaded isosurfaces","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=wilhelms van gelder octree","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=marching cubes node mesh generation","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=octree traversal surface extraction","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=edge tree isosurface","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1405773/?q=discrete marching cubes octree"],"cited_by":[{"path":"774-marching-cubes.md","name":"Marching Cubes","k":14},{"path":"1230-standard-interval-tree-for-isosurface-extraction.md","name":"Standard Interval Tree for Isosurface Extraction","k":2},{"path":"5619-empty-space-skipping-via-data-structures.md","name":"Empty Space Skipping via Data Structures","k":3},{"path":"6891-span-space-decomposition.md","name":"Span Space Decomposition","k":1},{"path":"6935-branch-on-need-octree-bono.md","name":"Branch-on-Need Octree (BONO)","k":1}]}